WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:01.126
♪♪

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:06.131
Lin:
I was a wanted man on the run
with no home in that first Bombay minute.

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.800
Lin:
Hope and cheer felt much the
same.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:09.968
♪♪

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:13.180
Shantaram is a book that
believes in the human spirit

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:16.141
Steve Lightfoot:
and so I was very excited when
the chance to adapt it came up.

00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:18.101
Charlie Hunnam:
I love this novel.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:19.770
I was blown away by the scope.

00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:22.105
By reading this book it made me
feel seen, 

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:26.193
it made me feel my
experiences in India mattered
and were relevant.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.778
♪♪

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:30.155
Steve Lightfoot:
Shantaram is a first-person
novel

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:32.741
being changed into a very
different storytelling form.

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:33.825
♪♪

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:37.162
They were going to do it as a
film but there is just no way
you can do justice 

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.206
Charlie Hunnam:
to this material in two and a
half hours. 

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.918
It needs the breadth and scale
and scope of a series.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.712
Lin:
I think freedom's all you can
ask for.

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:48.840
In the end, choice is all we
have.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:51.426
Charlie Hunnam:
Bombay nineteen eighty-one.

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:53.637
Charlie Hunnam:
The attention to detail and the
work that’s

00:00:53.637 --> 00:00:55.430
Charlie Hunnam:
been put into creating these
sets.

00:00:55.514 --> 00:00:58.141
Just the beauty of them. I mean
just [CHEF’S KISS].

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.894
Bharat Nalluri:
It’s an extraordinary feat to
pull off

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:03.981
but the real genius at the heart
of the series

00:01:04.106 --> 00:01:07.317
Bharat Nalluri:
is to find complex characters we
really care about.

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:10.279
Antonia Desplat:
All the characters are
multidimensional. 

00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:13.365
We really are diving in to see
all the worlds 

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:15.409
of those different people within
the same city.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:19.246
I felt the character "Lin" in my
heart and my soul.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.999
I can’t get involved in whatever
it is you guys do.

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:24.042
All the characters, 

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.712
Bharat Nalluri:
they’re all strangers in a
strange land 

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.714
Bharat Nalluri:
and they all have
their secrets and lies.

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:30.257
♪♪

00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:34.761
They’re all drawn to Indian
warmth and beauty of that
culture,

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:36.054
(All)
Hey!

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:39.224
but it’s also a dangerous place
and a dark place.

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:41.643
Only a fool plays a game without
knowing the rules first.

00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:42.978
♪♪

00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:46.064
Ultimately, that line between
good and evil

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:48.692
is the tightrope that the story
is walking.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.484
♪♪

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:51.194
Lin:
Here, maybe I get a second
chance.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.155
Lin:
A reckoning with my fate.

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:55.157
♪♪

